# UUID registration table and drain-before-reuse discipline

Models `KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::sessions_` (`SessionEntry{session, req_id, role}`
keyed by `uuid`) and its terminal sets (`done_sending_`, `done_recving_`,
`failed_recving_`) across duplicate announcements, conflicting UUIDs, inline
retirement, and poll sweeps. `recvTable` and `sendTable` partition the single
`sessions_` map by session type (`violatesExclusive`).

File aliases: `mgr.{h,cc}` = `tpu_sync/kv_cache/kv_cache_manager_with_transfer.{h,cc}`,
`recv.h` = `tpu_sync/kv_cache/transfer_receive_session.h`,
`send.h` = `tpu_sync/kv_cache/transfer_send_session.h`,
`reshard_{send,receive}.cc` = `tpu_sync/kv_cache/reshard_{send,receive}_session.cc`,
`send_drain_test.cc` = `tpu_sync/kv_cache/kv_cache_manager_with_transfer_send_drain_test.cc`,
`control_test.cc` = `tpu_sync/kv_cache/kv_cache_manager_with_transfer_control_test.cc`.

## State

| Field | C++ | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `recvTable` | `TransferReceiveSession` entries in `sessions_` | `Option RecvEntry` (`reqId`, `gen`, `recv : Recv`) per `uuid` |
| `sendTable` | `TransferSendSession` entries in `sessions_` | `Option SendEntry` (`reqId`, `gen`, `send : Send`) per `uuid` |
| `freeSlots` | `StagingBlockAllocator` free slots | conserved against `activeStaging recvTable` |
| `doneSending`, `doneRecving`, `failedRecving` | `done_sending_`, `done_recving_`, `failed_recving_` | terminal `req_id` sets reported by `CompleteReadWithDetails` |
| `nextGen` | ghost | monotonic generation counter distinguishing replaced sessions |

## Events

| Event | C++ |
|---|---|
| `startRead reqId uuid` | `StartRead(remote_endpoint)`: retires `Done()` incumbent inline; idempotent no-op if live receive has same `req_id`, else records `AlreadyExists` in `failed_recving_` |
| `registerRecv reqId uuid` | `RegisterRecv` / `EmplaceRecvSessionLocked`: finishes ready non-draining receive (`pollReady`), retires if `Done()`, else rejects (`RegisterActivePlan` skips finishing unsettled `plan()` incumbents) |
| `notifyForRead reqId uuid` | `NotifyForRead`: `sessions_.try_emplace` rejects any live or unretired `uuid` without retiring |
| `sweepRecv uuid` / `sweepSend uuid` | `CompleteReadWithDetails` / `CompleteReadRaw`: `RetireSettledSessionLocked` publishes and erases `Done()` entries under `SessionEntry::req_id` |
| `recvStep uuid e` / `sendStep uuid e` | per-session `Recv.Ev` / `Send.Ev` transitions (including sweep `pollReady` and `deadline() <= now` `cancel`) |

## Lock scopes

| Event | Scopes | Gap note |
|---|---|---|
| `startRead`, `registerRecv`, `notifyForRead`, `sweep*` | `KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::mu_` nesting session `mu_` and `StagingBlockAllocator::mu_` | `Done()` is monotone; candidates rejected by `EmplaceRecvSessionLocked` release staging in `~TransferReceiveSession` before unlock |
| `recvStep`, `sendStep` | session `mu_` scopes (`Receive.lean`, `Send.lean`) | see `Receive.lean` and `Send.lean` §Lock scopes |

## Properties

* **Slot conservation & session safety (`reachable_inv`, `reachable_recv_safe`, `reachable_send_safe`):**
  `freeSlots + activeStaging recvTable = cfg.numSlots` and `Recv.Safe` / `Send.Safe`
  hold on every reachable state.
* **Drain-before-reuse (`active_recv_preserved`, `active_send_preserved`):** an
  unsettled receive with `0 < inFlight` or `¬isReadyToComplete` (and any unsettled
  send offer) cannot be erased or have its `(reqId, gen)` replaced by any step;
  only a ready receive with `inFlight = 0` settles and is replaced in one
  `registerRecv` call (`trace_register_recv_replaces_ready_incumbent`).

